DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
"PGstandard.pl",
"MathObjects.pl",
"PGML.pl"
);
Context("Numeric");
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstantFunctions=>0);
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstants=>0);

$fun_2 = Formula("4*(x*2)");
$fun_1 = Formula("(x^2-2*x+3)^4");

Context("Interval");

$set_ans_4 = Compute("(((4, 8) - ((-infinity, infinity) - (4, 8))) - {-9, -8, -4, 8, 9})");
$set_ans_5 = Compute("(((4, 8)) - (3, 12))");
$set_ans_1 = Compute("{-2, 1} U (6, infinity)");
$set_ans_2 = Compute("{-2, 1} U (6, infinity) U (6, infinity)");
$set_ans_3 = Compute("{-2, 1} U {-2, 1}");

Context("Vector");

BEGIN_PGML
# Questions:

_For arithmetic problems, if the result is not an integer, then retain *three significant digits*._

Lily was organizing her book collection. She had [`16`] shelves in her room, each holding [`6`] books. In the living room, she had [`12`] shelves, each containing [`7`] books. How many books does Lily have in total?

[_____]{180}
[%
16*6+12*7

First, calculate the books in Lily's room: 16 × 6 = 96 books. Then, calculate the books in the living room: 12 × 7 = 84 books. Finally, add both amounts together: 96 + 84 = 180 books.
%]
---

During a baking day, Emma made cookies for her friends. She baked [`8`] chocolate chip cookies, [`3`] oatmeal cookies, and [`16`] sugar cookies. Then she found a small piece of cookie that was exactly one-seventh of a whole cookie. How many cookies did Emma have in total?

[_____]{27.1428571429}
[%
8+3+16+1/7

First, calculate the whole cookies: 8 + 3 + 16 = 27 cookies. Then, calculate the fractional part: 1 ÷ 7 = 0.142857... cookies. Finally, add them together: 27 + 0.142857... = 27.142857... cookies.
%]
---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{x | x > 5\}`]
- [`B = \{-2, 1\}`]

Compute:
- [`B \cup A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_1}
- [`B \cup A \cup A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_2}
- [`B \cup B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_3}

---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{x | 3 < x < 12\}`]
- [`B = \{-9, -8, -4, 8, 9\}`]
- [`C = \{x | 4 < x < 8\}`]

Compute:
- [`(C \cap C) - B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_4}
- [`(C) - A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_5}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -7, 4, 4 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle -8, -1, 9 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-8, -1, 9>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<-7, 4, 4>"))}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-7, 4, 4>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-7, 4, 4>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 9, 2, 0 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 6, 6, 1 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle 3, -5, 0 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{w} `]. [_____]{Compute("<3, -5, 0>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- [` \vec{v} \cdot \vec{w} = `] [_____]{Compute("<6, 6, 1>") . Compute("<3, -5, 0>")}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<6, 6, 1>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<6, 6, 1>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_1]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()}
- [`f'(2) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->eval(x=>2)}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->D()}
- [`f'(4) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->eval(x=>4)}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_2]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()}
- [`f'(5) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->eval(x=>5)}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->D()}
- [`f'(6) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->eval(x=>6)}

---
END_PGML
ENDDOCUMENT();
